From: mscharged-port
Subject: Draw the Mii model from its natively written vertex arrays
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84
Classification: native graphics ownership; the model draws as before.

RFLiInitCharModelRes builds a Mii model's vertex arrays (face, hair, cap,
nose, beard, mask and their normals and texture coordinates) with ordinary
stores into the RFLiCharModelRes at the start of the model's work buffer.
Natively, RFLDrawOpa/Xlu's GXSetArray goes through ChargedSetRFLGraphicsArray,
which resolves the address in the game allocation registry and refused those
arrays: they had neither graphics storage nor completed bytes. Once the
arrays are written, RFLiInitCharModel now publishes the struct as graphics
storage of native bytes (ChargedPublishRFLModelArrays). A model built again
in the same memory, such as the next Mii icon's work buffer, replaces the
earlier storage.

The positions and normals were already converted to native order while
copied; the texture coordinates were copied as the Wii's big-endian s16
pairs, which a native array would read as other coordinates (the face's
mask texture, with the eyes and mouth, then lay outside the face). They are
now converted too (ChargedCopyRFLShapeTexcoords). Console builds are
unchanged.

diff --git a/src/RVL_SDK/rfl/RFL_Model.c b/src/RVL_SDK/rfl/RFL_Model.c
index 2a871b2..7699ab2 100644
--- a/src/RVL_SDK/rfl/RFL_Model.c
+++ b/src/RVL_SDK/rfl/RFL_Model.c
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@
 #define RFL_SHAPE_HALF(pointer) ChargedReadRFLShapeHalf(pointer)
 #define RFL_SHAPE_S16(value) ChargedReadRFLShapeS16(&(value))
 #define RFL_SHAPE_VECTOR(destination, source) ChargedCopyRFLShapeVector(destination, source)
-#define RFL_SHAPE_BYTES(destination, source, bytes) ChargedCopyRFLShapeBytes(destination, source, bytes)
+#define RFL_SHAPE_BYTES(destination, source, bytes) ChargedCopyRFLShapeTexcoords(destination, source, bytes)
 #define RFL_TRANSFORM_RAW(destination, source) ChargedTransformRFLShapeCoordinate(destination, source)
 #else
 #define RFL_TEXTURE_HALF(texture, field) texture->field
@@ -252,6 +252,10 @@ void RFLiInitCharModel(RFLCharModel* model, RFLiCharInfo* info, void* work,
     }
 
     RFLiInitCharModelRes(imodel->res, info);
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE)
+    // The vertex arrays are written natively: RFLDrawOpa/Xlu draw from them.
+    ChargedPublishRFLModelArrays(imodel->res, sizeof(RFLiCharModelRes));
+#endif
 
     setExpr = FALSE;
     mipmap = FALSE;
